<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Simplifying and combining like surds through addition and subtraction</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify the following expression, giving your answer in the form \(a\sqrt{b}\), where \(b\) has no perfect-square factors:</p>
<p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;">\[ {@A@}\sqrt{{@m1@}} \;{@signchar@}\; {@Bmag@}\sqrt{{@m2@}} \]</p>
<p>\(a =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\(b =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Simplify each surd separately</b><br>
Find the largest perfect-square factor of each number inside the square root and apply \(\sqrt{x^2 \times y} = x\sqrt{y}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \sqrt{{@m1@}} = \sqrt{{@a1_sq@} \times {@p@}} = \sqrt{{@a1_sq@}} \times \sqrt{{@p@}} = {@a1@}\sqrt{{@p@}}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \sqrt{{@m2@}} = \sqrt{{@a2_sq@} \times {@p@}} = \sqrt{{@a2_sq@}} \times \sqrt{{@p@}} = {@a2@}\sqrt{{@p@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Substitute back and multiply the outside numbers</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@A@}\sqrt{{@m1@}} \;{@signchar@}\; {@Bmag@}\sqrt{{@m2@}} = {@A@}\left({@a1@}\sqrt{{@p@}}\right) \;{@signchar@}\; {@Bmag@}\left({@a2@}\sqrt{{@p@}}\right) = {@term1@}\sqrt{{@p@}} \;{@signchar@}\; {@term2@}\sqrt{{@p@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 3: Combine the like surds</b><br>
Both terms now share the same irrational part \(\sqrt{{@p@}}\), so combine their coefficients:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle ({@term1@} \;{@signchar@}\; {@term2@})\sqrt{{@p@}} = {@coeff@}\sqrt{{@p@}}\)</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {@A@}\sqrt{{@m1@}} \;{@signchar@}\; {@Bmag@}\sqrt{{@m2@}} = {@coeff@}\sqrt{{@p@}}, \quad \text{so } a = {@coeff@} \text{ and } b = {@p@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
